This file marks the directory beside it as Athena's own source checkout, so that
`athena.core.constitution` may read the `constitution/` next to this marker.

A running Athena reads her law from the copy shipped inside the wheel
(`athena/constitution/`, force-included by pyproject.toml) or from a frozen bundle. The checkout
is the third and last source, and it is guarded by this marker for one reason: without it, the
loader would walk three directories above `src/athena/core/` and read a `constitution/` out of
whatever happens to sit there — site-packages' parent, a PyInstaller extraction directory, a
temporary directory someone else can write into. A directory that merely contains a
`constitution/` is not Athena's source tree. This file says which one is.

See docs/adr/0006-two-output-prompt-composer.md.
